From 8d0b4b0e2b3c4d5e6f708192a3b4c5d6e7f809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saphira packaging <saphira@vm2.uk>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rpcbind lock file follows the split-/run layout

Upstream hardcodes RPCBINDDLOCK as /run/rpcbind.lock with no
configure knob (only --with-statedir is configurable, and it does
not cover the lock). Saphira keeps ordinary daemon state under
/var/run, so the lock moves with the state dir. The lock remains a
flat file (upstream shape preserved), now beside the state dir
instead of under the base runtime.

--- a/src/rpcbind.c
+++ b/src/rpcbind.c
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@
 /* who to suid to if -s is given */
 #define RUN_AS  "daemon"
 
-#define RPCBINDDLOCK "/run/rpcbind.lock"
+#define RPCBINDDLOCK "/var/run/rpcbind.lock"
 
 /* --- Write my pid to a file  (for debugging only?) --- */
 --
